{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_mc15_why_closed_expression_converted_why_closed_expression", "label": "Why a closed expression exists (reader-facing conversion)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/MC15-why-closed-expression.CONVERTED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Key citations resolved outward: L.closed to \u00a77.3, L.tree to \u00a78.5/\u00a711.4, L.box to \u00a710.4, K.three to Register 1175, K.helly to Appendix G Theorem 4.4 \u2014 the conversion is what lets a reader follow the argument without the key index."}, {"id": "recovered_mc15_why_closed_expression_converted_triangle_form_k3", "label": "The triangle form on K3 is join-closed but meet-broken", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/MC15-why-closed-expression.CONVERTED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "{|a-b| <= c <= a+b} on three coordinates is not a sublattice, and Lambda carries no such triple \u2014 zero of its thirty-five closing on three variables, the signature of a tree."}, {"id": "recovered_mc15_why_closed_expression_converted_helly_number", "label": "Lambda sits at the last graph structure where pairwise R is complete", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/MC15-why-closed-expression.CONVERTED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Helly number result (Appendix G, Theorem 4.4) places the tree of monotone binary bounds as the boundary case: Lambda closes in one pass where full arithmetic never closes."}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_mc15_why_closed_expression_converted_why_closed_expression", "target": "recovered_mc15_l_exact_three_necessary_conditions", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "recovered/MC15-why-closed-express